      "message": "I\u0027m at best neutral on this. We\u0027re replacing a Java standard call with an Android-shrinker-specific annotation, whose semantics are even less clear to me. In practice, I\u0027m sure either works. As far as the language spec is concerned, I think we have no guarantee that the containing NativeTombstoneManager object stays around, as opposed to the implementation just caching any fields it needs somewhere. I don\u0027t think ART pays attention to @Keep, so it could theoretically again get rid of the \"dead\" field assignment.\n\nI do agree that @Keep looks cleaner.\n\nI\u0027d be tempted to go with the \"belt and suspenders\" approach, and leave them both in.",
